            <ArticleTitle>Draft Genome Sequence of Aspergillus persii NIBRFGC000004109, Which Has Antibacterial Activity against Plant-Pathogenic Bacteria.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e00932-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.00932-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The fungus Aspergillus persii strain NIBRFGC000004109 is capable of producing penicillic acid and showed antibacterial activity against various plant-pathogenic bacteria, including Xanthomonas arboricola pv. pruni. Here, we report the first draft whole-genome sequence of A. persii The assembly comprises 38,414,373 bp, with 12 scaffolds.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017 Kim et al.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
